2101       data bballm;
2102       input School :$13. CSN DurhamSun DurhamHerald WashingtonPost
2103       USA_Today SportMagazine InsideSports UPI AP SportsIllustrated;
2104       label CSN = 'Community Sports News (Chapel Hill, NC)'
2105       DurhamSun = 'Durham Sun'
2106       DurhamHerald = 'Durham Morning Herald'
2107       WashingtonPost = 'Washington Post'
2108       USA_Today = 'USA Today'
2109       SportMagazine = 'Sport Magazine'
2110       InsideSports = 'Inside Sports'
2111       UPI = 'United Press International'
2112       AP = 'Associated Press'
2113       SportsIllustrated = 'Sports Illustrated'
2114       ;
2115       format CSN--SportsIllustrated 5.1;
2116       datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.BBALLM has 35 observations and 11 variables.

2152       ;
2153       * Find maximum rank for each news service and replace
2154       * each missing value with the next highest rank.;
2155       proc means data=bballm noprint;
2156       output out=maxrank
2157       max=mcsn mdurs mdurh mwas musa mspom mins mupi map mspoi;
2158       run;

NOTE: There were 35 observations read from the data set WORK.BBALLM.
NOTE: The data set WORK.MAXRANK has 1 observations and 12 variables.

2159       data bball;
2160       set bballm;
2161       if _n_=1 then set maxrank;
2162       array services[10] CSN--SportsIllustrated;
2163       array maxranks[10] mcsn--mspoi;
2164       keep School CSN--SportsIllustrated;
2165       do i=1 to 10;
2166       if services[i]=. then services[i]=maxranks[i]+1;
2167       end;
2168       run;

NOTE: There were 35 observations read from the data set WORK.BBALLM.
NOTE: There were 1 observations read from the data set WORK.MAXRANK.
NOTE: The data set WORK.BBALL has 35 observations and 11 variables.

2169       * Assume that the ranks are ordinal and that unranked teams would have
2170       * been ranked lower than ranked teams. Monotonically transform all ranked
2171       * teams while estimating the unranked teams. Enforce the constraint that
2172       * the missing ranks are estimated to be less than the observed ranks.
2173       * Order the unranked teams optimally within this constraint. Do this so
2174       * as to maximize the variance accounted for by one linear combination.
2175       * This makes the data as nearly rank one as possible, given the constraints.
2176       *
2177       * NOTE: The UNTIE transformation should be used with caution.
2178       * It frequently produces degenerate results.;
2179       ods graphics on;
2180       proc prinqual data=bball out=tbball scores n=1 tstandard=z
2181       plots=transformations;
2182       title2 'Optimal Monotonic Transformation of Ranked Teams';
2183       title3 'with Constrained Estimation of Unranked Teams';
2184       transform untie(CSN -- SportsIllustrated);
2185       id School;
2186       run;

WARNING: Failed to converge, however criterion change is less than 0.0001.
